WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.466
Harvest now, decrypt later is the risk that an attacker collects encrypted traffic or stored encrypted data today and saves it for possible decryption in the future.

2
00:00:10.466 --> 00:00:13.478
The attacker may not be able to read the data now.

3
00:00:13.478 --> 00:00:24.397
The concern is that future capability, including cryptographically relevant quantum capability, could expose data whose confidentiality still matters years from now.

4
00:00:24.397 --> 00:00:27.183
This risk depends heavily on data lifetime.

5
00:00:27.183 --> 00:00:35.089
If information only needs to remain confidential for minutes or days, future decryption years later may have limited value.

6
00:00:35.089 --> 00:00:40.586
If information must remain confidential for decades, the risk is much more important.

7
00:00:40.586 --> 00:00:53.236
Government data, healthcare records, legal records, intellectual property, trade secrets, critical infrastructure details, and sensitive personal information may all have long value windows.

8
00:00:53.236 --> 00:01:01.669
Encrypted network traffic is one area of concern, especially when sessions depend on quantum-vulnerable public-key key exchange.

9
00:01:01.669 --> 00:01:03.853
Stored encrypted data is another.

10
00:01:03.853 --> 00:01:13.039
Backups, archives, database dumps, document repositories, and captured files may remain sensitive long after the original system is retired.

11
00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:22.527
Security teams should understand which data has long confidentiality requirements and where encryption depends on vulnerable key establishment.

12
00:01:22.527 --> 00:01:25.689
The response is not panic collection of new tools.

13
00:01:25.689 --> 00:01:27.120
It is prioritization.

14
00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:33.295
Start with data that has long sensitivity, high adversary interest, and exposure to collection.

15
00:01:33.295 --> 00:01:38.565
Then identify the systems, protocols, certificates, keys, and vendors involved.

16
00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:48.580
Harvest-now-decrypt-later risk becomes manageable when it is tied to concrete data classes and migration plans rather than treated as a vague future worry.
